# Data, not branches

A generic algorithm reads specific data. Keep the algorithm short enough to describe. Make a change by changing the data it reads, not by adding an optional code block.

The schema is where a reader learns the categories of the problem. A field on `PatternInfo`, `Forest`, or a NamedTuple is a definition. It is not a comment beside a branch. If a category cannot be named on one of those records, do not add a special case yet.

Methide is the example. Repeat the split. Do not copy it as a one-off.

- The rule's data offers methide as an effect. There is no `pathways=("methide",)` flag and no block that turns methide on.
- Two methide ends resolve. A para-quinodimethane is two alkyl single-to-double ends. Do not add an `if` that refuses that pair. The one-side limit was a mistake.

An exception is allowed only with a good reason. Record it in `docs/forest/HEURISTICS.md` with `Status: approved`, `not approved`, or `not decided`. A silent branch is not an exception. None are approved.

Dropped behavior is recorded in `docs/forest/DROPPED.md` with the same status words. A listing there is not approval. Read the status before treating a cut as permanent.

Data may also say a rule is less likely. The schema for that is not decided. Do not invent the field. A later filter may read it. That is not an opt-in and not a branch.

This governs new work in this repo, especially `src/xenosite/forest/`. Do not retrofit `src/xenosite/_archive_forest/` unless asked.
